{
  "_readme": "Project Abyss devlog. 'milestones' is generated by tools/sync_abyss.py from the project's Plan.md; 'devlog' entries are written by hand, newest first.",
  "devlog": [
    {
      "date": "2026-10-25",
      "title": "Kick-off: swimming, and navigation in three layers",
      "tags": [
        "Player",
        "AI navigation",
        "Workflow"
      ],
      "text": [
        "First playable piece: the player swims in 3D in first person, towards where the camera looks, with ascend, descend and sprint, on keyboard and mouse as well as gamepad. Every speed is a tuning variable, and the player spawns directly in swimming mode.",
        "Biggest decision of the week: creature navigation is split into three layers, following Reynolds’ model. A Behavior Tree or State Tree decides what to do, an EQS query picks the next free waypoint towards that goal, and a steering component makes the creature swim there smoothly. EQS alone plans well but zigzags and stops at each point; steering alone is short-sighted. Together, the creature plans ahead and moves like it’s alive.",
        "Workflow: no Git LFS. Large third-party packs stay out of the repository, and work flows from a Programmation branch to Develop, then main."
      ]
    },
    {
      "date": "2026-10-24",
      "title": "Technical design and production plan",
      "tags": [
        "Planning"
      ],
      "text": [
        "Before any code: a Technical Design Document and a production plan. 16 weeks at 6 to 8 hours a week, every task between 2 and 4 hours with a clear “done when” criterion, and every milestone ending playable.",
        "The plan is honest about scope: the minimum viable demo fits in about 113 hours, the target version needs about 21 more. Cut lines and a freeze rule decide what gets dropped, not the deadline."
      ]
    }
  ],
